        "original_id": "3fc30149-1e46-5a73-9696-fedeaf28a8aa",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alberto Taquini\n- Projects: Taquini Plan\n- Places: Argentina\n- Topics: Higher education in Argentina, State education funding\n\nFacts:\n- In 1968, Alberto Taquini, a biochemist and academic, proposed the Taquini Plan in Argentina.\n- The Taquini Plan was also called the Plan de Creación de Nuevas Universidades or Plan Taquini.\n- The Taquini Plan was a project to restructure higher education in Argentina.\n- In Argentina, education in state institutions is free at the initial, primary, secondary, tertiary, and undergraduate university levels.\n- In Argentina, graduate programs at state institutions are not free.",
